    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f79a3b5_b2d042c8",
        "filename": "keystone/conf/fernet_receipts.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 10420
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-23T02:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m calling it fernet_receipts to match fernet_tokens.\n\nIf/when we introduce JWT tokens, we\u0027ll probably want to also introduce JWT receipts because it likely doesn\u0027t make sense to have a keystone with JWT tokens and Fernet Receipts, and a question that will crop up then is do we lock token and receipt provider types together.\n\nI also don\u0027t know if JWT will be using the same key directories (as in, will we rename it all to \u0027/etc/keystone/auth-keys/\u0027). In theory a key for fernet should also be compatible for JWT, but that discussion shouldn\u0027t happen here. We already have plenty of deployments using \u0027fernet-keys\u0027 and will need to transition, so that\u0027s a bigger discussion.",
      "parentUuid": "3f79a3b5_3308f425",
      "revId": "1514eaf699bfdd468229a80cbb89bda75ba20b30",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
